the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the aggregate cost is *an amount*.
    the customer price is *an amount*; scenario element.
    the discount type is *a text*; scenario element.
    the employee discount is *an amount*.
    the employee price is *an amount*; scenario element.
    the gross profit percentage is *a number*.
    the case is property.
    the case is services.
    the qualified employee discount is *an amount*.
    the aggregate cost given is *an amount*; scenario element.

the knowledge base cat_section_132 includes:


% Catala scope(s) QualifiedEmployeeDiscount — cat:section_132
the text of "(1) Qualified employee discount" is at "sources/us_tax_code/section_132.catala_en".

the text of "(3) Employee discount defined" is at "sources/us_tax_code/section_132.catala_en".

the text of "(1) Qualified employee discount; (A) In general" is at "sources/us_tax_code/section_132.catala_en".

the text of "Section 132" is at "sources/us_tax_code/section_132.catala_en".

rule aggregate_cost with provenance "(1) Qualified employee discount":
the aggregate cost is an amount N if
    the aggregate cost given is N
    otherwise the case is services
    and N = 0.

rule employee_discount with provenance "(3) Employee discount defined":
the employee discount is an amount N if
    the customer price is an amount M
    and the employee price is an amount K
    and N = M - K.

rule gross_profit_percentage with provenance "(1) Qualified employee discount; (A) In general":
the gross profit percentage is a number N if
    the case is services
    and N = 0
    otherwise the case is property
    and the customer price is an amount M
    and the aggregate cost is an amount K
    and N = (M - K) / M.

rule is_property with provenance "Section 132":
the case is property if
    the discount type is a text
    and the text is equal to "Property".

rule is_services with provenance "Section 132":
the case is services if
    the discount type is a text
    and the text is equal to "Services".

rule qualified_employee_discount with provenance "(1) Qualified employee discount":
the qualified employee discount is an amount N if
    the case is property
    and the employee discount is an amount M
    and the customer price is an amount K
    and the gross profit percentage is a number P
    and M > round(K * P * 100) / 100
    and the customer price is an amount Q
    and the gross profit percentage is a number R
    and N = round(Q * R * 100) / 100
    otherwise the case is property
    and the employee discount is N
    otherwise the case is services
    and the employee discount is an amount S
    and the customer price is an amount T
    and S > round(T * 0.2 * 100) / 100
    and the customer price is an amount U
    and N = round(U * 0.2 * 100) / 100
    otherwise the case is services
    and the employee discount is N.

scenario TestSection132_1 is, as stated in "sources/cat/section_132.test.yaml" at case 1:
    the aggregate cost given is 900.
    the customer price is 1500.
    the discount type is "Property".
    the employee price is 1000.
    q_employee_discount expects answers ["the employee discount is 500"].
    q_gross_profit_percentage expects answers ["the gross profit percentage is 0.4"].
    q_qualified_employee_discount expects answers ["the qualified employee discount is 500"].

